@@ BE8 | Hybrid
The price of copper falls by 30%, making the mining expansion much less profitable. What should the project manager do?
A) Re-evaluate the business case with the sponsor and consider options such as phasing or pausing
B) Continue as planned, since commodity prices always recover over the life of a mine
